# Symmetry-mode analysis (crystod-group --supergroup-cif); testsuite section 16
# AMPLIMODES-style decomposition of a group-subgroup distortion into parent irreps
# with mode amplitudes. References in ~/CrystOD-main/AMPLIMODES (Bilbao AMPLIMODES
# PDFs: SrTiO3 Pm-3m -> I4/mcm R5- 0.3303 A; ZrO2 Fm-3m -> P4_2/nmc X2- 0.5773 A).
#
# Since v0.3.4 every run also writes one VESTA file per activated irrep,
# {supergroup_file}_{irrep}.vesta, showing that irrep's displacement pattern as
# arrows on the parent-derived reference structure (invariant-core cell; the
# largest arrow is scaled to 1.5 A). The shipped 221_PPOSCAR_CaTiO3_*.vesta set
# (X5+/M2+/M3+/R4+/R5+) is the output of the CaTiO3 example:
#   crystod-group --supergroup-cif 221_PPOSCAR_CaTiO3.cif --subgroup-cif 62_PPOSCAR_CaTiO3.cif
# (see Symmetry_mode_analysis_CaTiO3.pdf for the Bilbao reference).
# The transcripts below predate the VESTA export and omit its closing section.

